.\" Man page for bifold(1). Keep the OPTIONS in sync with `bifold --help`:
.\" scripts/check-release-metadata.sh fails when a flag is undocumented here.
.TH BIFOLD 1 "2026-11-22" "Bifold" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bifold \- two\-pane file manager for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bifold
.RI [ PATH ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bifold
is a full\-screen, two\-panel file manager in the classic commander tradition:
the left pane is where you are, the right pane is where you are going.
Copy and move go from the active pane to the other one, in a background thread
with progress and cancel.
Deleting moves items to the trash by default.
.PP
The same program core drives the desktop front end,
.BR bifold\-gui (1).
Key bindings, colour themes and preferences are shared between the two.
.PP
Both panes start at
.I PATH
if one is given, otherwise at the folders remembered from the last session
(or the home folder).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-left " " \fIPATH\fR
Directory for the left pane.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-right " " \fIPATH\fR
Directory for the right pane.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Directory for both panes.
.TP
.B \-\-dump
Print both panes as plain text and exit, without starting the interface.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-keys
Print the effective key bindings as TOML and exit.
The output can be pasted into the configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Colour theme for this run only; it is not saved.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-themes
List the built\-in and user themes and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Ignore the configuration file and do not write one.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
These are the defaults; every one except those listed under
.B Fixed keys
can be rebound in the configuration file.
Press
.B h
inside the program for a tabbed help screen generated from the live bindings.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch the active pane.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Right ", " l
Enter a folder, view a file, or, on an executable, open an editable run line.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Backspace
Go to the parent folder.
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down ", " k ", " j
Move the cursor.
.TP
.B Space
Mark the entry and step down.
.BR Ctrl+A " / " Ctrl+D
mark all / clear marks.
.TP
.BR F2 ", " F3 ", " F4
Rename; view a file; view it as a hex dump.
.TP
.BR F5 ", " F6
Copy / move to the other pane.
.TP
.BR F7 ", " F8
New folder; delete (to the trash).
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
New file.
.TP
.B /
Filter the listing; plain text, or
.B *
and
.B ?
globs.
.TP
.BR g ", " r ", " .
Go to a path; refresh; show or hide hidden files.
.TP
.BR s ", " o
Cycle the sort key; flip the sort order.
.TP
.B t
Cycle the colour theme.
.TP
.B H
Show or hide the key\-hint line at the bottom of the screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Switch to the real terminal, as it is, and back (Enter, Esc or Ctrl+O returns).
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl+C
Quit.
.PP
In a text input,
.B Tab
completes folders, names, paths and programs on
.BR PATH ;
.B Shift+Tab
goes back through the candidates.
.PP
In the viewer,
.B x
toggles hex,
.B w
wraps lines and
.B Esc
closes.
.SS Fixed keys
.B h
(help), the dialog keys
.RB ( y / n ,
.BR Enter ,
.BR Esc ,
.BR Tab )
and the tab keys inside the help screen are not configurable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bifold/config.toml
Preferences and key bindings.
The directory is
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bifold
when that variable is set.
Bifold edits this file in place on exit and writes only the settings that
changed during the session; comments and unknown keys are kept.
A file that does not parse is reported at start\-up and never overwritten.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bifold/themes/NAME.toml
User colour themes; a theme may start from another with
.BR extends .
.TP
.I ~/.Trash
Where deleted items go (unless
.B delete_mode = "permanent"
is set).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the configuration, instead of
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B BIFOLD_TRASH_DIR
Use this folder as the trash instead of
.IR ~/.Trash .
.TP
.B HOME
Home folder: default start folder and the base of
.B ~
in paths.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on normal exit,
.B 1
on any error: an unknown option, a missing argument, or a terminal that cannot
be initialised (for example when standard input is not a terminal).
.SH EXAMPLES
Both panes in a project folder:
.PP
.RS
.B bifold \-\-path ~/src/project
.RE
.PP
Compare two folders:
.PP
.RS
.B bifold \-l ~/src \-r ~/Downloads
.RE
.PP
Try a theme without saving it:
.PP
.RS
.B bifold \-\-theme nord
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bifold\-gui (1)
.PP
